  "note": "Triennial election of the Limavady Urban District Council, 15 May 1936; only two nominations for nine seats, so the retiring members were deemed re-elected (Belfast Telegraph, 6 May 1936, p. 3). Only two nominations were received: Alexander Smyth (an old member) and Alexander Love (new). The eight retiring members were therefore deemed re-elected, with Love taking the place of the late James Wray, whose seat had been vacant since 1933. No party label was printed. The Northern Whig of the same date carries the same account. Returned unopposed.",
  "correctionNote": "Corrected from the page image of the Belfast Telegraph, 6 May 1936, p. 3 (council-audit, Nov 2026): Name_As_Printed 'Robt. Bloomfield' as printed (was 'Robert Bloomfield')."
